[{:db/id "q-1406/selection/6a10aed75783a1548ed61e712be1da722efc3de936946cd5e34ab166deb08f0b" :answer/id #uuid "f45aa475-1f0d-5466-a280-d5f4515a6c07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2i-11j+3k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1406/selection/3f09183fbd1f054309e7cd69aa3f7d653fbf3c1dae6f39dd88e49429f534f443" :answer/id #uuid "bc1295d6-b73a-54af-993e-65d79d4f7be8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2i-11k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1406/selection/71f931079bd813b9f19ffde7b26d6e00d85c6cb414795c3d34d709787474ae0a" :answer/id #uuid "87f4a9da-d670-5548-8de3-3731a8f934a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2i+3k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1406/selection/b24dde319d5f4b0d6fb2ac7f4921e4bb5800093eafdece13874d1c49bc87e111" :answer/id #uuid "4c280daa-d711-5a22-be18-23769f14a9ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7i-11j+3k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1406/selection/d3c7dfa939cfd7899d56e3e89defbd89a48020450968061b4a2230f3af7c9f9a" :answer/id #uuid "81f3ea0f-8e86-5379-a4ff-f7c27d44191e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2i+11j-5k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1406/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fc2bd0f-4423-520e-978d-b504a808bdde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-1406/selection/6a10aed75783a1548ed61e712be1da722efc3de936946cd5e34ab166deb08f0b" :answer-field/choices ["q-1406/selection/6a10aed75783a1548ed61e712be1da722efc3de936946cd5e34ab166deb08f0b" "q-1406/selection/3f09183fbd1f054309e7cd69aa3f7d653fbf3c1dae6f39dd88e49429f534f443" "q-1406/selection/71f931079bd813b9f19ffde7b26d6e00d85c6cb414795c3d34d709787474ae0a" "q-1406/selection/b24dde319d5f4b0d6fb2ac7f4921e4bb5800093eafdece13874d1c49bc87e111" "q-1406/selection/d3c7dfa939cfd7899d56e3e89defbd89a48020450968061b4a2230f3af7c9f9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1406" :question/id #uuid "427de437-0817-5025-a19d-93d24fc75213" :question/math-academy-id "q-1406" :question/problem "Let $u=3i-2k$ and $v=-2i+j+5k.$ Determine $u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-(3\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+(3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =(0+2)i-(15-4)j+(3-0)k \\\\  & =2i-11j+3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1406/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1406"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19786"] :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{13}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(6x-8)j+(0-2)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-(6x-8),-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-(6x-8))^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36{x}^{2}-96x+64+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ \\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77} & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+77 & =13 \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+64 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-24x+16 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-4 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{4}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-282262/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "d08227f9-7fb9-57e1-b24b-04d7717315df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186303495 :answer-field/choices ["q-282262/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282276/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "175571ef-5a37-57f7-8fef-095de8fcfbaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282276/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6c65aa6-e71f-5d1a-9f30-d21c749bb924" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282276/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-282276/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282276/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "294c6f86-d2d4-5dfb-ad67-518e235aa1d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282276/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0aa99fc5-7859-59c5-a94a-5a4598cca902" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282276/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-282276/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282276" :question/id #uuid "8782e145-18ba-5261-8ddf-00ef3416804e" :question/math-academy-id "q-282276" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,4,5⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{33}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4-0)i-(x-5)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4,5-x,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(5-x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+(25-10x+{x}^{2})+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57} & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+57 & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+24 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=4,$ $x=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-282276/field-1" "q-282276/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282276"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
